/*****************************************************************************
    jitElseT -- the POP for jitEmitGIF's ELSE ARM, added 2026-07-31.
    Its sibling is incant/jitThenT. READ THE ONE-TESTING-PER-FILE NOTE BELOW
    BEFORE MERGING THEM BACK TOGETHER, because that is exactly what this
    fixture's first draft did and it produced a convincing false red.

    WHAT IT IS FOR. Until 2026-07-31 `jitEmitGIF` declared only `ExpressioN:`
    and `StatemenT:` -- no `ElsE:` -- while `aCTionIF` declared all three. So a
    jitted if/else NEVER VISITED its else statement: not emitted, not
    interpreted, it vanished. A false condition then left the target untouched
    and returned garbage, AT EXIT 0, with no diagnostic of any kind.

    That was the only WRONG ANSWER AT EXIT 0 in the JIT, and a wrong answer with
    a clean exit outranks every crash on the list -- a crash is at least visible.

        testIfElse code={ if righty > 0; maximus = righty * 2; else maximus = 7; }

    THIS FILE RUNS THE FALSE CONDITION, which is the informative direction:

        righty = -7  ->  maximus = 7     ELSE arm reached
                         maximus = 11    the OLD BUG (neither arm ran)
                         maximus = 26    would mean the wrong arm ran

    Init is maximus = 11, so the fixture tells all three outcomes apart rather
    than merely passing or failing.

    ⚠ THE TAKEN CASE IS IN jitThenT AND IS NOT EVIDENCE ON ITS OWN. It was
    ALREADY GREEN before the else arm existed, because it exercises only the arm
    that was emitted -- it was CORRECT BY LUCK. A fixture running only the taken
    case would have reported success against a defect that made the other half
    return garbage.

    ⚠⚠ ONE `testing()` PER FILE, AND THIS FIXTURE PAID FOR THAT RULE TWICE.
    A SECOND generate on the same action in the same run hits the documented
    sequential-state-corruption tar baby (CLAUDE.md Testing). The first draft of
    this file ran both directions in one process and reported the then arm as
    11 -- a REGRESSION THAT DID NOT EXIST. Re-run alone, the same case gives 26.
    So the split into two files is a correctness requirement, not tidiness, and
    a merged version will produce a red that looks exactly like a real one.

    IR, cheaply:
        INCANT_JIT_DUMP=1 <binary> incant/jitElseT 2>&1
    Expect FOUR blocks -- entry, then, else, endif -- with the condition
    branching to then/else and both arms storing to the same baked field
    address before branching to endif.

    SENTINEL AT THE FOOT (standing harness rule H2).
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);

search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities list;

righty  = 0 - 7;
maximus = 11;
print "else-arm setup : righty =" righty " maximus =" maximus:;
testing(testIfElse);
print "else-arm result: maximus =" maximus " (want 7; 11 = the old bug; 26 = wrong arm)":;

print "JE SENTINEL -- run reached the end":;
stop();
